dsh-better-git-worktree — third-party notices
=============================================

## @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace

`client.js` is generated by `scripts/build-client.mjs` and **inlines the client
half of `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace`** as shipped in this deployment's
`node_modules`, with a small set of exact-string "seams" applied (see the
`decorateOfficialWorkspaceClient` function). The package is MIT licensed:

    @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace
    Copyright (c) DeepSeek
    MIT License — https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness

Why the copy is necessary rather than a dependency: the harness exposes the
sidebar browsing region as a `single` Slot, and the child seat it declares
(`sidebar.workspaces.directoryFlow`) can only be rendered by the entry that
declared it. A wrapper registered *beside* the official entry therefore cannot
render that child, and re-declaring the children table throws. The only
supported shape is to stand in for the entry — which means owning its client,
which means inlining it. `dsh-git-worktree` reaches the same conclusion and
solves it with build-time virtual modules; this plugin solves it with a plain
generated bundle.

The seams are exact-string patches and fail closed: an unverified
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace` version, or a drifted generated shape,
makes `node scripts/build-client.mjs` error out with the seam name instead of
silently producing an undecorated sidebar.

Nothing in `node_modules` is modified. The official loader row is disabled
in-memory while this plugin is active and restored to its composed `disabled`
option on teardown.

Working copies themselves are plain `git worktree add` checkouts — no third-party
code is involved in creating or managing them.
